            <ArticleTitle>Pseudotumor cerebri presenting with ataxia and hyper-reflexia in a non-obese woman treated with sinus stenting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/neurintsurg-2011-010073</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To report a successful treatment of an atypical case of pseudotumor cerebri.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Pseudotumor cerebri is a disorder of raised intracranial pressure. Multiple Case Series have been published about its treatment with sinus stenting. All these cases have had typical presentations.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">An atypical fulminant case of pseudotumor cerebri which was treated successfully with venous sinus stenting.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Venous sinus stenting can be done effectively in atypical cases of pseudotumor cerebri.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
